id: pm-4vwcvq
title: "GH-772: rejected extension command registration leaves silent partial activation and zero-exit command gaps"
description: "When one extension command registration is rejected, earlier siblings remain active while the rejected and later commands disappear; invoking a dropped command yields misleading parent help or arity output with exit zero, and extension manage reports unknown activation state."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T14:04:33.678Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T15:03:26.789Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T18:20:01.079Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Rejected command registration cannot leave an undisclosed partially active surface; manifest-declared unavailable commands return a stable nonzero diagnostic; extension manage and help expose exact runtime activation status; real packed-extension tests cover rejection before, within, and after sibling command registrations."
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-ugqx
reporter: github-issue-772
severity: high
environment: pm 2026.7.27 with a command extension that collides with a host-owned global flag
repro_steps: "Install pm-csv@2026.7.23 in a fresh workspace, inspect install diagnostics and extension manage, then invoke csv validate help and csv validate."
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Activation is atomic; unavailable declared paths fail nonzero with the cause; manage reports live activation truth.
actual_result: "Packed pm-csv@2026.7.23 proof returns exit 2 for both dropped paths with the flag-collision cause, and manage reports failed/false."
component: "extensions:command-registration"
