  "2026-07-27T14:04:33.678Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches for GH-772 and partial activation found the closed visibility owner pm-yffj and command-dispatch lineage but no item covering atomic registration,zero-exit dropped paths,or manage status parity."
  "2026-07-27T14:07:57.427Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/772. Canonical PM link was posted on the issue; this PR includes tracker-only triage and does not claim or implement the open report."
  "2026-07-27T16:42:42.527Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: active in the shared runtime-capability-contracts bundle. Duplicate check covered all 2,136 tracker items and live GitHub reports; this item owns a distinct acceptance facet and will share exact-head verification with the related active items."
  "2026-07-27T18:19:10.846Z","harness:codex","Evidence: activation is transactional across every registry. Real packed @unbrained/pm-cli consumer with pm-csv@2026.7.23 proved install exit 1, dropped help exit 2, dropped run exit 2, and both command diagnostics include pm-csv's rejected --json activation cause. Default extension manage reports runtime_active=false and activation_status=failed. Unit rollback tests cover failures before/within/after sibling registrations; CLI integration passes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T18:19:11.587Z","harness:codex","Rollback the complete registry set at the extension boundary, then reuse unknown-command recovery for stable nonzero diagnostics; default manage probing keeps lifecycle truth aligned with health and command recovery."
